& [SourcePreservation]
  + raw continuation intent is separately preserved and digest-pinned before canonicalization
  + no implementation authority is inferred from the preceding Slice9 completion alone

& [Delineation]
  + Slice9 remains the pure semantic registry and Slice7 remains lifecycle judgment owner
  + Slice10 owns only MCP decoding bounded summaries and one synchronized volatile process-local registry value
  + the closed stateless Slice8 server remains unchanged

& [DualHemisphereReview]
  + [expansive] compact calls make repeated multi-pass inference interaction practical and provide the first usable content-handle bridge
  + [analytic] one closed tagged command avoids three separate recursive tool schemas while exact response unions preserve operation differences
  + [reconciliation] register once then validate by handle is admitted while retained-body readback durable storage and hidden reconstruction remain absent

& [HonestyAndSecurity]
  + adapter success is transport/state success and cannot upgrade an inner lifecycle refusal
  + registry digests are concurrency and integrity coordinates rather than credentials
  + serialized mutation under one mutex provides process-local atomicity only

& [Decision]
  + [status] accepted_for_canonicalization_and_phase_lock
  + [implementation_shape] separate cantor_compiler_custody_mcp crate with one stdio tool and one volatile registry
